{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A remembrance of teru'ah.</b> A remembrance of the teru'ah of a king, in which they rejoice in their king, as it says: הַרְנִינוּ לֵאלֹהִים עֻזֵּנוּ הָרִיעוּ (Psalms 81:2). This is because He then sits on the throne of judgment, as received in tradition, as it says: תִּקְעוּ בַחֹדֶשׁ שׁוֹפָר בַּכֶּסֶה לְיוֹם חַגֵּנוּ, כִּי חֹק לְיִשְׂרָאֵל הוּא מִשְׁפָּט לֵאלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב (Psalms 81:4–5). And it is fitting for us to rejoice then all the more, because He is our king who inclines toward mercy, and acquits us in judging us, as it says: כִּי ה׳ שֹׁפְטֵנוּ, ה׳ מְחֹקְקֵנוּ, ה׳ מַלְכֵּנוּ הוּא יוֹשִׁיעֵנוּ (Isaiah 33:22)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:36.515737394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}